From f6baaa78680c23d7dd0be4c802c372d0d75c97bc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 12:32:05 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] vulkan: vertex cache keeps whole buffers and tracks guest
 writes instead of hashing

Mario Kart 7 draws hundreds of pieces out of a few multi-megabyte vertex buffers per frame; the
per-draw copy (and the hash of it) moved ~10 GB/s. A buffer is now copied once, as one block
covering every range drawn from it, and kept until the game, a DMA or a GPU transfer writes to
the guest pages it came from (watched through the rasterizer cache's page counters). Buffers
rewritten right after being copied go back to per-draw uploads for a while. Arenas the current
draw points into are never recycled under it (the old cache could, which corrupted draws with
more than one vertex buffer: characters in Mario Kart 7).
